Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 00:05:41 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] feat(sniff): detect BitTorrent DHT and UDP trackers, and
 take no DNS for uTP

From Jolymmiles/Xray-core: a routing rule protocol ["bittorrent"] missed
the DHT (BEP 5) and UDP trackers (BEP 15), the UDP a torrent client
speaks first, and SniffUTP could take a DNS query for a uTP ST_SYN. The
bittorrent package is taken as it is there (48ba2a9e, d771af92, eeb7ea9b,
57216346, a7ef1450, 81df5002), and the dispatcher runs SniffDHT and
SniffUDPTracker after SniffUTP.

The dispatcher tests come along: the bittorrent validation tests, the
end-to-end test that blocks torrent traffic on a real Xray process while
DNS, plain UDP and TCP pass, and the QUIC test that sniffing leaves the
cached datagrams as they came, with the Hysteria corpus it reads. A test
file gives them the names Joly's dispatcher has.

